  "description": "<p>fedora-rebuild should take two exclusive arguments, 1) list of directories and 2) list of pids. In the case of the list of directories, fedora-rebuild would rebuild in depth-first order.</p>\n\n<p>For example, fedora-rebuild.sh -d /opt/fedora/data/objectStore/2011/10 /opt/fedora/data/objectStore/2011/11 would recursively rebuild all of the objects found in those two directories.</p>\n\n<p>Alternatively, fedora-rebuild.sh -p demo:123 demo:abc would rebuild the two objects specified.</p>\n\n<p>Rationale: For a large repository, rebuild takes hours, if not days, during which system is unavailable. In a disaster-recovery scenario, we'd like to be able to get back online with at least the \"most important\" objects rebuilt as soon as possible.</p>\n\n<p>This also allows for selective recovery in the case of isolated inconsistencies that are detected.</p>\n\n<p>Finally, this mechanism would allow for parallel rebuild processes to further speed the rebuild time.</p>",
